// What an inserted beat has before its when block: a persistent state, which
// only initializes once, a temporary state, which initializes at every
// insertion, a line of text, which plays during the collection, and an
// assignment. Each of them runs the same way at every pick.

state
  ready: true

beat Start
  Talk()
  Talk()
  Talk()

beat Talk
  when
    + Counted
    + Fresh
    + Chatty
    + Setter
    true
      Talk fallback.
  Talk done.

beat Counted
  state
    visits: 0
  visits += 1
  when
    visits == 1
      Counted once.
    visits == 2
      Counted twice.
    visits > 2
      Counted $visits times.

beat Fresh
  new state
    seen: 0
  seen += 1
  when
    seen == 1
      Fresh every time.
    seen > 1
      Fresh kept its state.

beat Chatty
  Chatty prologue.
  when
    ready
      Chatty rule.
  Chatty epilogue.

beat Setter
  ready = true
  when
    ready
      Setter rule.

/*
<test>
- expected: |
    ~ Chatty prologue.

    ~ Counted once.

    ~ Talk done.

    ~ Chatty prologue.

    ~ Counted twice.

    ~ Talk done.

    ~ Chatty prologue.

    ~ Counted 3 times.

    ~ Talk done.
</test>
*/
